<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm6a-yaogan50-03 ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 6A / Yaogan 50-03 — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
NO public LM-6A time/altitude/velocity table found. Loft: SURROGATE — LM-3B typical GTO trajectory, CALT &#x27;LM-3A Series Launch Vehicles User&#x27;s Manual&#x27; Issue 2011, Tables 3-5/3-6
(event time s, flight altitude km, ground range km), liftoff altitude 1.8 km removed. Cut at Stage-3 first shutdown T+615.7 s, 204.3 km, 2466.2 km.
Source: http://www.georing.biz/usefull/LM-3A%20Series%20Launch%20Vehicles%20User&#x27;s%20Manual%20Issue%202011.pdf
Ground range IS published, so no Rel.Vel split is needed; velocities are d/dt of interpolated alt/range (rel_vel = |v| ground-relative).
One horizontal assumption: LM-3B&#x27;s published ground range is laid along this mission&#x27;s constant-azimuth rhumb (LM-3B itself doglegs).
LM-6A is a kerosene/LOX core + solid boosters (different family): LOW confidence in loft AND azimuth.
Az 190 deg is a guess (no published hazard azimuth used). Mission flown: LL2 Success, orbit LEO.
Pad (LL2): 38.858300N 111.580200E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=190.00 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-10-23T10:15:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
<Placemark><name>Pad (lm6a-yaogan50-03)</name><Point><coordinates>111.5802000,38.8583000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
